        "Enhanced recovery is a bundle — education and prehabilitation, anaemia and nutrition corrected, smoking stopped four weeks before; clear fluids and a carbohydrate drink until two hours before, no bowel preparation or sedative premed; minimally invasive surgery, regional and opioid-sparing analgesia, goal-directed fluid, warming, no routine tube or drain; eating and two hours out of bed on day 0, six hours on day 1, catheter and drip out on day 1, regular paracetamol and anti-inflammatory, discharge by criteria — and compliance with the whole bundle, which is nursing, cuts complications by a third.",
